nat46: export is_map_t_dev for qca-nss-ecm MAP-T support

qca-nss-ecm enables its MAP-T interface support whenever kmod-nat46 is
selected (ECM_INTERFACE_MAP_T_ENABLE) and then references is_map_t_dev()
from nat46. Upstream nat46 does not provide it. Add a minimal exported
predicate (reusing the existing NAT46 device signature check) so ecm links.

Self-contained and generated against the current nat46 (no old-version pin,
no radix-tree machinery), so it applies with zero fuzz under quilt.

--- a/nat46/modules/nat46-core.h
+++ b/nat46/modules/nat46-core.h
@@ -82,4 +82,6 @@
 nat46_instance_t *alloc_nat46_instance(int npairs, nat46_instance_t *old, int from_ipair, int to_ipair, int remove_ipair);
 void release_nat46_instance(nat46_instance_t *nat46);

+bool is_map_t_dev(struct net_device *dev);
+
 #endif
--- a/nat46/modules/nat46-netdev.c
+++ b/nat46/modules/nat46-netdev.c
@@ -199,6 +199,16 @@
 	return (priv && (NAT46_DEVICE_SIGNATURE == priv->sig));
 }

+bool is_map_t_dev(struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	nat46_netdev_priv_t *priv;
+	if (!dev)
+		return false;
+	priv = netdev_priv(dev);
+	return (priv && (NAT46_DEVICE_SIGNATURE == priv->sig));
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(is_map_t_dev);
+
